    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8283df44-6e71-507c-89a8-b5de0c97456e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-5 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{1}:=R_{1}+(2)\\cdot R_{2}$ on $V?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{1}:=R_{1}+(2)\\cdot R_{2}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V &= \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-5 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}:=R_{1}+(2)\\cdot R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-5+(2)(9) & 6+(2)(-6) & 3+(2)(9) \\\\ 9 & -6 & 9\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}13 & -6 & 21 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
