      ":question/id": "2aa1b295-810a-53e8-b486-3d7b4e81edeb",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $N,$ given by\n\n$$\nN=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-7 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 9 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -5 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{2}:=R_{2}+(2)\\cdot R_{3}$ on $N?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{2}:=R_{2}+(2)\\cdot R_{3}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nN=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-7 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 9 & -7 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -5 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{2}:=R_{2}+(2)\\cdot R_{3}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\sim {\\scriptsize \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-7 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 3+(2)(-1) & 1+(2)(-1) & 9+(2)(-5) & -7+(2)(-8) \\\\ -1 & -1 & -5 & -8\\end{array}\\right]}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-7 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 & -23 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -5 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
