      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 9 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 7 & -8 \\\\ -7 & -8 & -5 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{1}:=R_{1}+(-1)\\cdot R_{3}$ on $M?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{1}:=R_{1}+(-1)\\cdot R_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the first row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 9 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 7 & -8 \\\\ -7 & -8 & -5 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}:=R_{1}+(-1)\\cdot R_{3}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\sim {\\scriptsize \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6+(-1)(-7) & 9+(-1)(-8) & 8+(-1)(-5) & 9+(-1)(-2) \\\\ 3 & 7 & 7 & -8 \\\\ -7 & -8 & -5 & -2\\end{array}\\right]}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}13 & 17 & 13 & 11 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 7 & -8 \\\\ -7 & -8 & -5 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
